          "children" : [ {
            "children" : [ {
              "attributes" : {
                "dxpStyle" : { },
                "imageInfos" : "",
                "richTextValue" : "<h2>Introduction</h2>\n\n<p>Our tours start with an introduction at our main facility. Your tour guide will introduce you to ginseng and our company, then ask questions \n    to tailor the tour specific to each group. During this time, you will be introduced to ginseng, learn the differences between American and \n    Asian ginseng and understand the history of ginseng and our company.</p><br>\n\n<h2>Step Into Our Ginseng Gardens</h2>\n\n<p>We have several fields of ginseng at different ages and stages of the growth cycle depending on the month or season of your visit. \n    Experience one of our ginseng gardens in person. Learn about the unique growth cycle of American ginseng, \n    field prep, and cultivation challenges of this specialty crop.</p><br>\n\n<h2>Visit Our Farm Facilities</h2>\n<p>We have several fields of ginseng at different ages and stages of the growth cycle depending on the month or season of your visit. \n    Experience one of our ginseng gardens in person. Learn about the unique growth cycle of American ginseng, field prep, and \n    cultivation challenges of this specialty crop.</p><br>\n\n<h2>Discover Our Headquarters</h2>\n<p>At Hsu’s Ginseng, we have a brokerage and export business process built on over 50 years of trust and personal relationships with local \n    farmers and foreign buyers. You will learn how Paul Hsu started this process in the basement of his home. \n    Our headquarters is also home to our production area for many of our packaged products found on Chinatown store shelves and airport gift shops. \n    You will understand production challenges as well as discover our products.</p>"
              },
              "definition" : "community_builder:htmlEditor",
